From 0a2565bc7251a158dcf4ca7251a9c91106be73c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:11:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Screen sleep and the lid: backlights off after idle or when
 closed

docs/SLEEP-LOCK-PLAN.md steps 2 and 3 (light sleep). screensleep.c: a
1 s timer turns the backlights off after nds_sleep_secs (default 120)
without local input, through the ARM7's FIFO_POWER_CMD_BACKLIGHT_POWER
(the power chip's backlight bits, as DSLinuxs ndsbl). button.c and
nds_ts.c report every new press with nds_screen_activity(); the press
that wakes the screen is held back until released, so waking never
clicks or types. The lid (the ARM7's hinge bit, button.c) turns the
screen off at once when closed and on when opened. Programs keep
running. /proc/dsisettings: "sleep N" (0 = never, max 3600), "screen
off" / "screen on"; the read line gains sleep=, screen=, lid=.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
